  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: An upper level low centered along the\ncentral Oregon coastline early this morning will keep a\nsouthwesterly flow aloft across Nevada. The main impacts this\nafternoon and early evening from the approaching system will be \ngusty southerly winds for most of central and portions of \nnortheastern NV. Strongest winds today are expected across White \nPine County where southerly winds of 10 to 20 mph and gusts to 30 \nmph are likely. Higher terrain can expect slightly higher wind \nspeeds. Dry and storm-free conditions are expected across the CWA\ntoday, along with slightly below temperatures. The upper level low\nto our NW will weaken tonight into Sunday as it moves onshore\nthrough southern Oregon and northern California, with scattered\nrain showers and isolated thunderstorms across mainly the northern\nand eastern portions of the CWA Sunday afternoon and early\nevening. A few light rain showers mainly over mountain areas\nSunday night as the upper level low weakens into a trough and\nexits east through Idaho. Dry conditions are expected across the\nCWA Monday and Tuesday. Wednesday through next weekend there will\nbe increasing chances of precipitation as trough energy approaches\nfrom the Pacific NW, while at the same time remnants of what is\ncurrently hurricane Marie in the Eastern Pacific Ocean well\noffshore of Baja Mexico, begins to feed additional moisture up\ninto the southwestern US through CA and likely into NV.  \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in cool\ntemperatures and gusty winds through the weekend. Low confidence \nin storm potential next week. No changes were made from the NBM \nforecast.",
